# Devcontainer pin upgrade blocklist — one <base> per line to HOLD a tool in
# .devcontainer/Dockerfile at its current `ARG <BASE>_VERSION` pin instead of
# tracking upstream latest.
#
# Base names match the Dockerfile ARG <BASE>_VERSION, lowercased, and must be one
# the gate actually watches (scripts/lib/devcontainer-pin-sources.ts):
#   bw
#
# NOTE: do NOT add an entry for a release that is merely too fresh.
# scripts/check-devcontainer-pin-freshness.ts reads `minimum-release-age` from
# .npmrc and automatically defers anything published inside that window — the
# hold clears itself once the version ages out. Only blocklist a pin held back
# for a real reason (a breaking change, a broken asset, an upstream regression).
#
# Each entry needs a substantive BLOCKER reason (>=30 chars, no banned phrases),
# exactly like every other suppression list in this repo. Format:
#
#   # BLOCKER: <why this tool is pinned back and when to revisit>
#   <base>
#
# Empty by default — nothing is held; every pin tracks upstream.
